From 24b6d105cee175fcc40d6a5cf7130621a84a7840 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:31:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] unloaded sweeper + producer admission: host pass
 under host_loop_lease, per-process residual for live chats
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Design t_01a1d45d75851804 §2b (R1-R4), card t_01a1d471722af0cf. kanban_unloaded._loop was 14.9% of a steady hub
serve's samples (10.1% of the gateway's) and producer_admission._loop 3.9%: every gateway, Desktop serve and
dashboard process ran both host-wide sweeps.

- kanban_unloaded: the loop holds lease 'kanban-unloaded' (role gateway > serve > dashboard from the process
  kind). The holder runs the host pass (remote + local sweeps, delegation and guarantee for every chat,
  notice_fanout.card_change_pass, killed-subagent retry over every profile store) and beat()s; every other
  process runs a residual pass, delegation_unloaded.sweep_once(only=live) and guarantee_pass(only=live), for the
  chats it holds itself (those return skipped:held from any other process).
- Wake capacity: the holder gets 8 slots per pass kind (HERMES_KANBAN_HOLDER_WAKE_SLOTS); a standby or the
  kill switch keeps 2. Out of slots, the local sweep rewinds the claim and the remote sweep releases its ledger
  claim (deferred:slots), retried next pass instead of a passive row, until OVERDUE_S (then the row, as before).
  The per-chat wake budget is counted by the holder, so it is now in effect host-wide.
- notice_fanout: cursors and the remote snapshot live in <kanban home>/kanban/notice-fanout.db, so a lease
  hand-off resumes the interval instead of re-seeding (memory fallback when the file can't open).
- producer_admission: sweep_once only in the 'producer-admission' lease holder; deliver_pending unchanged.
- HERMES_HOST_LOOP_LEASE=0 restores per-process passes.

Tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_kanban_unloaded_host_lease.py (RED on the base: routing, residual, exactly-once,
hand-off, slots, every-store retry, producer gate, roles).
